\image{conf-njit-rtch-coil.jpg}

\p{\strong{Caption.} A cost-effective, 3D-printed \strong{6-DOF robotic TMS coil holder} (Prusa Mk4S, PLA + PETG carbon fiber; high-torque servos + rotary encoders) meant to replace manual coil-holding for long sessions — reducing operator fatigue and coil drift. Target: hold a ~2.5 kg TMS coil within a few mm / few degrees over hours. The low-cost, in-house-manufacturable counterpart to the commercial Axium Cobot in [[conf-stanford-tms-navinibs]].}
